HST Office: live preview of a paragraph style in the document while the pointer rests on it in the
ribbon Styles gallery (Writer), as in Word.

Owner decision (2026-11-07): the hover live preview ships on; the StyleHoverPreview switch
(org.openoffice.Office.HSTRibbon, hst-ribbon-switches.patch) is rollback safety only.

- svx/source/tbxctrls/StylesPreviewWindow.cxx, svx/source/inc/StylesPreviewWindow.hxx: after 300 ms
  over a style the style is set on the paragraphs of the selection; leaving the style or the gallery,
  clicking (which then applies the style for real) or closing puts the previous styles back. Both
  steps run with the undo manager locked, change tracking suspended and the modified state frozen
  (XModifiable2), so the document stays unmodified, the undo and redo stacks are unchanged, no change
  is tracked and autorecovery sees nothing to save. A save, a store-to (autorecovery) or an unload
  ends the preview before the document is written. Read-only documents, non-text selections and
  selections of more than 200 paragraphs get no preview; protected text puts everything back.

